simple method, but caches all subqueries too\n  for(int i=0; i<=amount ~/ coinTypes[0]; i++){\n    count += 
cachedCoins(amount-(i*coinTypes[0]),coinTypes.sublist(1));     // sublist(1) is like lisp's '(rest ...)'\n  }\n\n  /// add this to the 
